@@ -15,3 +15,26 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Readers sign in at `/signin` with a username and password (verified server-side against the
+Times account service) or with a passkey. Once signed in, **Account settings** (`/account`,
+also linked from the header and the footer's "Manage My Account") lets readers:
+
+- add a passkey (WebAuthn registration via `@simplewebauthn`),
+- rename passkeys, and
+- remove passkeys they no longer use.
+
+Changes are mirrored to the browser's authenticator through the WebAuthn Signal API
+(`PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials()` / `signalCurrentUserDetails()`), and a
+sign-in attempt with a passkey the server no longer knows triggers `signalUnknownCredential()`
+so the browser can delete the stale credential.
+
+Passkey records are stored in a JSON file. Relevant environment variables:
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `PASSKEY_STORE_PATH` | `./data/passkeys.json` | Where passkeys and user handles are persisted. |
+| `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` | request hostname | Relying Party ID, if it must differ from the served host. |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` | request origin | Expected origin for WebAuthn ceremonies. |
